      "disposition": "CONFIRMED",
      "file": "src/code_forge/machine.py",
      "line_range": [
        493,
        493
      ],
      "description": "[qodo] Setting `daemon=False` prevents the Python process from returning asynchronously. The interpreter blocks on exit until all non-daemon threads have completed. As a result, the CLI process (and the CI step running it) will hang for the duration of the mutation operation instead of delegating it to the background. Consequently, the mechanism for out-of-band monitoring using `mutation-result.json` is entirely negated. To properly branch off a background job that outlives the current process, a detached subprocess (e.g., via `subprocess.Popen` with appropriate flags to sever it from the session) must be used instead of standard threading.",
      "error": null,
      "anchor": null,
      "evidence_files": null,
      "is_timeout": false
    },
    {
      "id": "l1-qodo-ed629c0708660750",
      "fingerprint": "ed629c0708660750",
      "source": "L1",
      "disposition": "UNCERTAIN",
      "file": "tests/test_machine_mutation_launch.py",
      "line_range": [
        81,
        81
      ],
      "description": "[qodo] This test codifies a flawed assumption about Python threading logic. It explicitly tests that the thread is spawned with `daemon=False` based on an incorrect premise that doing so allows it to run asynchronously while the review process returns. As noted, a non-daemon thread will indefinitely block the main interpreter's exit.",
      "error": null,
      "anchor": null,
      "evidence_files": null,
      "is_timeout": false
    },
    {
      "id": "l1-expert-86e900124c145beb",
      "fingerprint": "86e900124c145beb",
      "source": "L1",
      "disposition": "UNCERTAIN",
      "file": "src/code_forge/machine.py",
      "line_range": [
        493,
        493
      ],
      "description": "[expert] Using `daemon=False` for the background execution thread causes the CLI process to block indefinitely on exit, as Python's `sys.exit()` joins all non-daemon threads. This completely defeats the architectural intent of an \"async\" measurement and will cause `code-forge review --mode ci` to hang for ~10+ minutes. Furthermore, since threads share the process PID, tracking `os.getpid()` is flawed for detecting whether this background task is still alive across runs, because the PID tracked is just the CLI's PID. You should spawn a completely detached background OS process (e.g., using `subprocess.Popen` with `start_new_session=True` or a double-fork daemonization) rather than trying to outlive the main process with a thread.",
      "error": null,
      "anchor": null,
      "evidence_files": null,
      "is_timeout": false
    },
    {
      "id": "l1-expert-6832a0398019cf10",
      "fingerprint": "6832a0398019cf10",
      "source": "L1",
      "disposition": "UNCERTAIN",
      "file": "tests/test_machine_mutation_launch.py",
      "line_range": [
        81,
        81
      ],
      "description": "[expert] The test explicitly enforces `daemon is False` to ensure the mutation completes, which enforces the bug causing the CLI to hang. When the mutation logic is refactored to spawn a separate OS process, this test will need to be rewritten to assert process detachment constraints (e.g. `start_new_session=True`) rather than thread configuration.",
      "error": null,
      "anchor": null,
